PART 40 — The 10 Answers You Should Memorize

If you have limited preparation time, memorize these:

1. LangChain

Framework for building LLM applications using models, prompts, tools, retrieval, structured output and agents.

2. LangGraph

Low-level runtime for orchestrating stateful, long-running agent workflows with state, routing, persistence, durable execution and human-in-the-loop.

3. Agent

An LLM-driven system that dynamically decides which tools/actions to use to accomplish a goal.

4. RAG

Retrieval-Augmented Generation retrieves relevant external information and supplies it to the LLM as context before generation.

5. Tool

A callable function exposed to an LLM so it can interact with external systems or perform deterministic operations.

6. State

Shared execution context containing the information required by graph nodes to make decisions and produce updates.

7. Checkpointer

Persistence mechanism that saves graph state at execution steps, enabling memory, recovery, HITL and time travel.

8. Thread

Persistent execution identity used to associate checkpoints with a conversation/workflow.

9. HITL

A workflow pattern where execution pauses for human review and resumes after the human provides a decision.

10. LangSmith

Observability and evaluation platform used to trace, debug and evaluate LLM and agent executions.

